        "end": 595,
        "quote": "Von Hippel-Lindau (VHL) disease a familial cancer syndrome characterized by benign or malignant tumors and cystic lesions affecting multiple systems. It may present with hemangioblastomas in the brain, spinal cord, and retina; renal cysts and clear cell renal cell carcinoma; pheochromocytoma; pancreatic cysts and neuroendocrine tumors; endolymphatic sac tumors; and epididymal and ligamentum latum cysts. . . . VHL was suspected based on the presence of multiple, bilateral retinal hemangioblastomas and history of cerebral hemangioblastoma. VHL gene sequence analysis revealed a heterozygous "
      },
